III
Abstract
As a modern and efficient mode of urban rail transport, the metro plays an important role
in urban development. With the increase of urban population and traffic demand, the metro
system is constantly expanding and improving. However, due to the large scale of metro
construction, complex construction process and high technical requirements, there are various
potential safety risks in the construction process. The construction risks caused by different
risk factors occur frequently, resulting in certain casualties and property losses. How to
structure and systematically store the metro construction safety experience regarding case
knowledge, expert experience and the knowledge in the specification, and realise the
automatic identification of construction safety risk through knowledge management and rule
reasoning for the characteristics of different types of workmanship, should be a new idea to
solve this problem. Based on this, in order to solve these problems that constrain the
development of metro, this study introduces ontology technology and knowledge
management into the field of metro construction safety risk management, and develops a
related domain ontology. Through the establishment of a metro construction safety risk
ontology knowledge base is used to achieve the reuse, update and formal representation of
risk knowledge to support safety risk identification and the adoption of appropriate safety
measures to prevent and reduce the occurrence of risk events. The study of metro construction
safety risk knowledge ontology has the following important significance: (1) The organisation
and structured representation of risk knowledge in the field of metro construction safety
management. (2) As a basis for indexing and retrieval of metro construction safety documents.
(3) To achieve semantic integration and interoperability of heterogeneous systems. The main
work of this paper is as follows:
(1) Analyse and summarize the current research status of construction safety
management at home and abroad, point out the shortcomings of the current domestic research,
and conclude that how to realize the effective preservation and sharing of empirical
knowledge is an important way to improve the current shortcomings of metro construction
safety management. On this basis, by analysing the current status of the application of
precursor information theory, information technology and knowledge management in
construction safety management, the research objectives of the thesis are defined, and the
content and technical route of the thesis are clarified.
(2) The precursor information system is constructed based on the theory of accident
causation. For different types of construction methods, such as open cut method, cover cut
method, shield method, etc., the work breakdown structure method is applied to decompose


